  title "Operational Security"
  summary "In a tense negotiation beneath Midway Shelf, Niaecum~ of ☽'ofund' Guild navigates competing interests between the Cell (a declining authority with a cracked seal), Sanctcateia~ (a Cell negotiator seeking access to ancient tunnel maps), and The Gore Emissary (a Wake-Singer orca representative mapping the deep). When the Cell attempts to coerce Niaecum~ into a joint endorsement that would surrender her guild's secret routes, she instead shares cartography directly with The Gore Emissary, establishing an alliance that bypasses both the Cell and the Midnight Claws who control Ravium's thermal vents. The Cell responds by sealing corridors and cutting off fire-core supplies, but Niaecum~'s name is carved into stone as a registered entity, and the Wake-Singers begin learning penguin tunnel architecture, shifting the balance of power in the deep while something ancient stirs beneath Ravium's corrupted ice."
